index=entra (sourcetype="azure:loganalytics:signinlogs" OR sourcetype="azure:loganalytics:aadnoninteractiveusersigninlogs") UserPrincipalName="bg-admin-*" earliest=-1h latest=now
``` ========================================================================== ```
``` Detection (SPL): Break-glass (emergency access) account sign-in - ANY sign-in ```
``` Lab:             Contoso Health Identity Platform - Splunk second SIEM        ```
``` KQL twin:        lab/kql/break-glass-signin.kql (same logic/window/columns)   ```
``` -------------------------------------------------------------------------- ```
``` STAND-IN: runs on the Splunk Enterprise 60-day TRIAL (replaces production   ```
``` Splunk) over Entra logs REPLAYED from Log Analytics by                      ```
``` lab/splunk/ingest-from-loganalytics.sh (replaces the Splunk Add-on for      ```
``` Microsoft Azure / Event Hub streaming).                                     ```
```                                                                            ```
``` WHY THE BASE SEARCH IS LINE 1: Splunk breaks a search that starts with a    ```
``` comment before its first (generating) command, so every .spl file in this  ```
``` folder opens with its base search and the commentary follows it.           ```
```                                                                            ```
``` WHAT IT CATCHES                                                             ```
```   ANY authentication - success OR failure, interactive OR non-interactive - ```
```   by an emergency-access account (bg-admin-01 / bg-admin-02). They hold     ```
```   standing Global Administrator and are excluded from CA and PIM, so every  ```
```   sign-in is high-signal (threshold = 1 row).                               ```
```                                                                            ```
``` KQL -> SPL TRANSLATION                                                      ```
```   union SigninLogs, AADNonInteractive...  -> two sourcetypes OR-ed in the   ```
```                                              base search                    ```
```   extend SignInType = "interactive"/...   -> eval on sourcetype             ```
```   where TimeGenerated > ago(1h)           -> earliest=-1h latest=now        ```
```   matches regex @"(?i)^bg-admin-\d{2}@"   -> regex command, same pattern    ```
```                                              with [0-9] for \d (KQL runs    ```
```                                              RE2, whose \d is ASCII-only,   ```
```                                              so the two are equal;          ```
```                                              no backslash to escape). The   ```
```                                              bg-admin-* base term is only a ```
```                                              cheap pre-filter               ```
```   tostring(LocationDetails.countryOrRegion) -> spath path=...               ```
```   project ... | sort by TimeGenerated desc -> sort 0 - _time | table ...    ```
```   (_time IS TimeGenerated: the replay sets the HEC "time" from it.)         ```
```                                                                            ```
``` NOTE: AADNonInteractiveUserSignInLogs stores LocationDetails as a STRING    ```
``` column holding JSON (SigninLogs stores it as dynamic). The replay parses it ```
``` so both sourcetypes expose the same nested LocationDetails.* path here.     ```
```                                                                            ```
``` SCHEDULE: mirrors the Sentinel rule in lab/terraform/modules/monitoring     ```
``` (frequency PT5M, lookback PT1H, severity High, trigger > 0 rows, 1 h        ```
``` grouping by the Account + IP entities -> per-result throttle below).        ```
``` The @stanza / @conf lines are read by render-savedsearches.sh to build      ```
``` app/contoso_identity/default/savedsearches.conf; Splunk ignores them.       ```
``` OBJECT IDS (2026-11-07): the KQL twin also matches the accounts' immutable ```
``` object ids (UserId in BreakGlassUserIds), so a renamed account still       ```
``` alerts in Sentinel. This Splunk stand-in has no break-glass id lookup yet, ```
``` so it matches the naming convention only and says so in MatchedBy. The    ```
``` UserId column is carried so a reviewer sees the id that matched there.    ```
``` ========================================================================== ```
``` @stanza Contoso - Break-glass account sign-in (any) ```
``` @conf description = Any sign-in (interactive or non-interactive, success or failure) by an emergency-access account. Always investigated by a second admin. KQL twin: lab/kql/break-glass-signin.kql ```
``` @conf disabled = 0 ```
``` @conf enableSched = 1 ```
``` @conf cron_schedule = */5 * * * * ```
``` @conf dispatch.earliest_time = -1h ```
``` @conf dispatch.latest_time = now ```
``` @conf counttype = number of events ```
``` @conf relation = greater than ```
``` @conf quantity = 0 ```
``` @conf alert.track = 1 ```
``` @conf alert.severity = 5 ```
``` @conf alert.expires = 7d ```
``` @conf alert.digest_mode = 0 ```
``` @conf alert.suppress = 1 ```
``` @conf alert.suppress.fields = UserPrincipalName,IPAddress ```
``` @conf alert.suppress.period = 1h ```
``` @conf request.ui_dispatch_app = search ```
``` @conf request.ui_dispatch_view = search ```
| regex UserPrincipalName="(?i)^bg-admin-[0-9]{2}@"
| eval SignInType=if(sourcetype=="azure:loganalytics:signinlogs", "interactive", "non-interactive")
| eval MatchedBy="naming convention"
| spath path=LocationDetails.countryOrRegion output=Country
| sort 0 - _time
| table TimeGenerated, SignInType, UserPrincipalName, UserId, MatchedBy, IPAddress, Country, AppDisplayName, ClientAppUsed, ResultType, ResultDescription, ConditionalAccessStatus, CorrelationId
